The system prompt
-----------------

system.txt is the profile's system prompt (plan 019 section 3.6), and, as of
plan 029 section 3.2 L1, it is craze's own text, written for this tool set —
not opencode's default.txt, which it replaced. Nothing in it is ported the
way the descriptions above are; it is drafted, reviewed and kept on its own
merits (plan 029's evaluation harness, section 3.1). Its three placeholders,
${workspace}, ${os} and ${shell}, are the session's workspace, runtime.GOOS
and the path of the shell the bash tool runs commands with (opencode.Shell(),
the shell bash's own description also names, by its basename); nothing else
varies, so every request in a session still starts with the same bytes (D-30).
No clock or git state is in it.

Some of its sentences read close to a sentence in one of three reference
prompts the plan asked to be compared against, because the idea and the
words it is put in are both worth keeping; where that is so, the source is
recorded below. An idea alone — something every one of these tools' prompts
says in its own words, such as "run the tests before you claim to be done" —
is not recorded; only a sentence whose wording is recognizably close to a
specific source sentence is. Nothing here is copied source code, and no
sentence is reproduced whole from a reference: each is craze's own sentence,
shaped like the tools around it, adapted for a wording that is close to one
listed:

